<title>USA: US senator urges soft approach in EU grain talks.</title>
<headline>US senator urges soft approach in EU grain talks.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Senate agriculture committee chairman Richard Lugar Thursday urged diplomacy to avoid a new grain subsidy war with the European Union.</p>
<p>&quot;If we're diplomatically successful we'll stop (the EU) from doing that,&quot; Lugar said, referring to the possibility of EU wheat dumping.</p>
<p>&quot;If we don't spend that much time on trade...we'll have some problems again,&quot; Lugar, R-Ind., added.</p>
<p>Speaking at the annual conference of the U.S. National Broiler Council, the senator repeated his opposition to the resumption of U.S. Export Enhancement Program subsidies.</p>
<p>USDA trade adviser Paul Drazek is currently in Europe for talks on grain trade and other issues.</p>
</text>
